IMPORT prelude

-- Duties Act 1997 (New South Wales) -- transfer duty on a home or residential land, the First Home Buyers Assistance
-- Scheme, the spouse exemption, surcharge purchaser duty and motor vehicle registration duty.
--
-- SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE. The rules are written in the Act's own actors and terms: "the transferee", "the purchaser or
-- transferee", "the applicant", "the applicant for registration". The buyer's questions are in nsw-duties-seat.l4,
-- which IMPORTs this module and restates no rule. Computations are functions; where the text says "must" or sets a
-- deadline there is a regulative rule (DEONTIC), five in all, in the last section.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: Chapter 2: s 8 (duty charged on a transfer or agreement for transfer of dutiable property),
-- s 11(1)(a) (land in NSW is dutiable property), s 12 (when liability arises), s 13 (the transferee pays), s 14 (joint
-- tenants as tenants in common in equal shares), ss 15, 16, 16A (written statement, lodging, purchaser's declaration,
-- within 3 months: regulative), s 17 (no tax default if paid within 3 months: regulative), s 21 (dutiable value), s 32
-- (general rate, as a table), s 32A (premium rate; residential land in s 32A(3) worked out from facts), ss 33AB-33AF
-- (indexation: s 33AC and s 33AD as functions; s 33AF amounts as inputs); Part 8 Division 1, ss 70, 71, 73, 73A, 74(1)-
-- (3), 75, 76, 76A, 78A(1) (First Home Buyers Assistance Scheme); s 78B(1), (2), (6) (when the shared equity concession
-- is in play); Part 8 Division 4, ss 104A, 104B, 104C (spouse transfers; the s 104C factor is an input); Chapter 2A,
-- s 104J (foreign person: a fact), s 104K, s 104I (residential land), s 104R, s 104U, s 104V, s 104W (regulative),
-- s 104ZK(2); Chapter 9, ss 261, 262 (regulative), 263, 264, 265, 266, 267(1), (6), (6A), (7), (7A), (7AA), (7B), 268.
--
-- NOT COVERED (an explicit `not covered` answer, asserted in the cases): the concessional duty formulas in s 78A(2) and
-- (2A) and the shared equity formula in s 78B(3), whose formula images the corpus dropped (only the where-clauses
-- survive); ss 32B and 32C; s 104C beyond a supplied apportionment factor; s 104ZB, s 104ZKA and s 104ZKB; a liability
-- before 1 July 2019 (general rate), an agreement before 1 July 2023 (the scheme, Schedule 1 cl 147(3)) or a surcharge
-- liability before 1 January 2025 (the deposit's version date; the 9% rate's commencement is not in the deposit).
--
-- Edition: Duties Act 1997 No 123 (act-1997-123), corpus version 2025-01-01, from the Open Australian Legal Corpus as at
-- 10 March 2025, deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/act-1997-123.txt. NOT THE CURRENT OFFICIAL TEXT; IT MAY BE
-- OUT OF DATE. The s 32 table in the deposit holds the 2019-20 base amounts; later years' amounts come from s 33AC and
-- s 33AD, or from the Chief Commissioner's s 33AF notice (not deposited).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Duties Act 1997 (NSW) -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `Arithmetic used by the rates`

-- "for every $100 (or part)": a part of $100 counts as a whole $100. Nothing is counted for an amount of $0 or less.
GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of 100-dollar parts in` MEANS
    IF `amount` AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF FLOOR (`amount` DIVIDED BY 100) TIMES 100 EQUALS `amount`
         THEN `amount` DIVIDED BY 100
         ELSE FLOOR (`amount` DIVIDED BY 100) PLUS 1

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- s 33AC(2): "A/B is calculated to the nearest 3 decimal places (and a fourth decimal place of 5 is to be rounded up)".
GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`to the nearest 3 decimal places, 5 up` MEANS
    FLOOR (`x` TIMES 1000 PLUS 0.5) DIVIDED BY 1000

-- s 33AC(3): "rounded to the nearest $1,000 (and an amount of $500 is to be rounded up)".
GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`to the nearest 1000 dollars, 500 up` MEANS
    FLOOR (`x` DIVIDED BY 1000 PLUS 0.5) TIMES 1000

-- s 33AD(3): "rounded to the nearest dollar (and an amount of 50 cents is to be rounded down)".
GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`to the nearest dollar, 50 cents down` MEANS
    0 MINUS FLOOR (0.5 MINUS `x`)

§§ `Dates`

-- Dates use the prelude's built-in DATE functions only (no IMPORT of daydate).
-- READING: "within 3 months after" a day ends on the same day of the month 3 months later, or on that month's last
-- day where it is shorter (30 November to 28 February). The Interpretation Act 1987, which would settle it, is not
-- deposited.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in the month of` MEANS
    DATE_SERIAL `the first of the next month` MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (DATE_MONTH `the day`) (DATE_YEAR `the day`))
    WHERE
        `the first of the next month` MEANS
            IF DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 12
            THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS 1)
            ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (DATE_MONTH `the day` PLUS 1) (DATE_YEAR `the day`)

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day that is` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (`the smaller day`) `the month` `the year`
    WHERE
        `months from year zero` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the day`) TIMES 12 PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS `months`
        `the year` MEANS FLOOR (`months from year zero` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the month` MEANS `months from year zero` MINUS (`the year` TIMES 12) PLUS 1
        `the smaller day` MEANS
            IF DATE_DAY `the day` AT MOST `the number of days in the month of` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 `the month` `the year`)
            THEN DATE_DAY `the day`
            ELSE `the number of days in the month of` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 `the month` `the year`)

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days from the day to` MEANS
    DATE_SERIAL (`the day that is` `the day` `months`) MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the day`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `d` IS A NUMBER, `m` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day is on or after` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the day` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY `d` `m` `y`)

-- The financial year that begins on 1 July of the year returned: 1 July 2019 to 30 June 2020 is 2019.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the financial year of` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `the day` AT LEAST 7 THEN DATE_YEAR `the day` ELSE DATE_YEAR `the day` MINUS 1

§§ `Answers that carry an amount, or say why there is none`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `the liability arose before 1 July 2019, before the s 32 table in the deposit applied`
    `the amounts given for the year cannot be amounts adjusted under s 33AC`
    `s 32B applies: residential land above the premium threshold used for other purposes; its apportionment factor is not encoded`
    `s 32C applies: a parcel of residential land of more than 2 hectares above the premium threshold; not encoded`
    `the s 78A(2) or (2A) concessional duty formula is missing from the deposited text`
    `the s 78B(3) shared equity concession formula is missing from the deposited text`
    `the agreement or transfer is before 1 July 2023, to which the Act as in force before the First Home Buyer Legislation Amendment Act 2023 applies (Schedule 1 cl 147(3)); not deposited`
    `the land has a building under construction or more than one dwelling, which the scheme's two cases (a private dwelling, a vacant block) do not plainly cover`
    `the surcharge liability arose before 1 January 2025, the version date of the deposit; the commencement of the 9% rate is not in the deposit`
    `a foreign transferee may be an exempt permanent resident or retirement visa holder (s 104ZKA, s 104ZKB); not encoded`
    `the land is used for other purposes and the s 104ZB apportionment factor is not encoded`

DECLARE `Duty answer` IS ONE OF
    `the duty is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `s 21 -- the dutiable value`

-- s 21(1): "The dutiable value of dutiable property that is subject to a dutiable transaction is the greater of-- (a) the
-- consideration (if any) for the dutiable transaction ..., and (b) the unencumbered value of the dutiable property."
-- s 22: the consideration includes encumbrances; s 23: the unencumbered value disregards them. Both are inputs.
GIVEN `the consideration` IS A NUMBER, `the unencumbered value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the dutiable value of the property` MEANS
    `the greater of` `the consideration` `the unencumbered value`

§§ `s 32 and Part 3 Division 3 -- the general rate and its indexation`

-- s 32(1): "the base amount for the threshold range that applies ... plus the amount determined at the fixed rate".
--   Range  Minimum     Maximum     Base amount  Fixed rate
--   1      $0          $14,000     $0           $1.25 for every $100 (or part) of the dutiable value
--   2      $14,000     $30,000     $175         $1.50 for every $100 (or part) by which the DV exceeds the minimum
--   3      $30,000     $81,000     $415         $1.75 ...
--   4      $81,000     $304,000    $1,307       $3.50 ...
--   5      $304,000    $1,013,000  $9,112       $4.50 ...
--   6      $1,013,000  --          $41,017      $5.50 ...
-- s 32(2): a range applies if the DV "is more than the minimum threshold amount but not more than the maximum".
-- s 32(4): each minimum and maximum threshold amount is an adjustable amount (Division 3). The base amounts are adjusted
-- under s 33AD; the fixed rates are not adjusted. The table's amounts are those "that applied before any adjustment"
-- (s 33AC(2)), that is, for the year beginning 1 July 2019 (the s 32A note gives that year's premium base amount).
DECLARE `Threshold range` HAS
    `minimum threshold amount` IS A NUMBER
    `base amount` IS A NUMBER
    `fixed rate per 100` IS A NUMBER

-- The table, highest range first: the first range whose minimum the dutiable value exceeds is the one that applies.
`the s 32 table as deposited` MEANS
    LIST `Threshold range` OF 1013000, 41017, 5.50
         `Threshold range` OF 304000, 9112, 4.50
         `Threshold range` OF 81000, 1307, 3.50
         `Threshold range` OF 30000, 415, 1.75
         `Threshold range` OF 14000, 175, 1.50
         `Threshold range` OF 0, 0, 1.25

GIVEN `table` IS A LIST OF `Threshold range`
      `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the duty at the general rate on` MEANS
    CONSIDER `table`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN `range` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN
        IF `the dutiable value` GREATER THAN `range`'s `minimum threshold amount`
        THEN `range`'s `base amount`
             PLUS `range`'s `fixed rate per 100` TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`the dutiable value` MINUS `range`'s `minimum threshold amount`)
        ELSE `the duty at the general rate on` `rest` `the dutiable value`

-- The adjustable amounts for a year: the minimum threshold amounts of ranges 2 to 6 (each also the maximum of the range
-- below; range 1's minimum is $0) and the s 32A premium threshold ($3,040,000, s 32A(2C)).
DECLARE `Adjustable amounts` HAS
    `range 2 minimum` IS A NUMBER
    `range 3 minimum` IS A NUMBER
    `range 4 minimum` IS A NUMBER
    `range 5 minimum` IS A NUMBER
    `range 6 minimum` IS A NUMBER
    `premium threshold` IS A NUMBER

`the amounts before any adjustment` MEANS
    `Adjustable amounts` OF 14000, 30000, 81000, 304000, 1013000, 3040000

-- s 33AC(2): the amount for a year is the amount "that applied before any adjustment under this Division" multiplied by
-- A/B, where A is the Sydney CPI number (s 33AB) "for the March quarter in the year immediately preceding the year for
-- which the amount is calculated" and B is the CPI number "for the March quarter of 2019". (3): rounded to the nearest
-- $1,000. (4): "if the adjustable amount calculated for any year is less than the amount that applied for the previous
-- year, then the amount for that previous year applies instead." A and B are not in the deposit: inputs.
GIVEN `the amount before any adjustment` IS A NUMBER
      `A` IS A NUMBER
      `B` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount for the previous year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 33AC adjusted amount` MEANS
    `the greater of` (`to the nearest 1000 dollars, 500 up` (`the amount before any adjustment` TIMES `to the nearest 3 decimal places, 5 up` (`A` DIVIDED BY `B`)))
                     `the amount for the previous year`

GIVEN `A` IS A NUMBER, `B` IS A NUMBER, `the previous year's amounts` IS AN `Adjustable amounts`
GIVETH AN `Adjustable amounts`
`the adjustable amounts for the year` MEANS
    `Adjustable amounts` OF
        `adjusted` (`the amounts before any adjustment`'s `range 2 minimum`) (`the previous year's amounts`'s `range 2 minimum`),
        `adjusted` (`the amounts before any adjustment`'s `range 3 minimum`) (`the previous year's amounts`'s `range 3 minimum`),
        `adjusted` (`the amounts before any adjustment`'s `range 4 minimum`) (`the previous year's amounts`'s `range 4 minimum`),
        `adjusted` (`the amounts before any adjustment`'s `range 5 minimum`) (`the previous year's amounts`'s `range 5 minimum`),
        `adjusted` (`the amounts before any adjustment`'s `range 6 minimum`) (`the previous year's amounts`'s `range 6 minimum`),
        `adjusted` (`the amounts before any adjustment`'s `premium threshold`) (`the previous year's amounts`'s `premium threshold`)
    WHERE
        `adjusted` `base` `previous` MEANS `the s 33AC adjusted amount` `base` `A` `B` `previous`

-- s 33AD(1): each base amount is "equal to the sum of all fixed rate amounts determined for the preceding threshold
-- ranges"; (2): the fixed rate amount for a range is "the amount determined at the fixed rate in respect of dutiable
-- property that has a dutiable value equal to the maximum threshold amount for the threshold range"; (3): rounded to
-- the nearest dollar, 50 cents down. The sum is of the unrounded fixed rate amounts; only the base amount is rounded.
GIVEN `amounts` IS AN `Adjustable amounts`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Threshold range`
`the general rate table for` MEANS
    LIST `Threshold range` OF (`amounts`'s `range 6 minimum`), (`to the nearest dollar, 50 cents down` (`f1` PLUS `f2` PLUS `f3` PLUS `f4` PLUS `f5`)), 5.50
         `Threshold range` OF (`amounts`'s `range 5 minimum`), (`to the nearest dollar, 50 cents down` (`f1` PLUS `f2` PLUS `f3` PLUS `f4`)), 4.50
         `Threshold range` OF (`amounts`'s `range 4 minimum`), (`to the nearest dollar, 50 cents down` (`f1` PLUS `f2` PLUS `f3`)), 3.50
         `Threshold range` OF (`amounts`'s `range 3 minimum`), (`to the nearest dollar, 50 cents down` (`f1` PLUS `f2`)), 1.75
         `Threshold range` OF (`amounts`'s `range 2 minimum`), (`to the nearest dollar, 50 cents down` `f1`), 1.50
         `Threshold range` OF 0, 0, 1.25
    WHERE
        `f1` MEANS 1.25 TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`amounts`'s `range 2 minimum`)
        `f2` MEANS 1.50 TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`amounts`'s `range 3 minimum` MINUS `amounts`'s `range 2 minimum`)
        `f3` MEANS 1.75 TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`amounts`'s `range 4 minimum` MINUS `amounts`'s `range 3 minimum`)
        `f4` MEANS 3.50 TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`amounts`'s `range 5 minimum` MINUS `amounts`'s `range 4 minimum`)
        `f5` MEANS 4.50 TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`amounts`'s `range 6 minimum` MINUS `amounts`'s `range 5 minimum`)

-- Every amount s 33AC can produce is a multiple of $1,000 that is not below its 2019-20 amount: the 2019-20 amounts are
-- multiples of $1,000, s 33AC(3) rounds to $1,000, and s 33AC(4) never lets an amount fall below the year before. Amounts
-- given for a later year (from the s 33AF notice) that fail this cannot be that year's amounts.
GIVEN `amounts` IS AN `Adjustable amounts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the amounts could be amounts adjusted under s 33AC` IF
        `possible` (`amounts`'s `range 2 minimum`) (`the amounts before any adjustment`'s `range 2 minimum`)
    AND `possible` (`amounts`'s `range 3 minimum`) (`the amounts before any adjustment`'s `range 3 minimum`)
    AND `possible` (`amounts`'s `range 4 minimum`) (`the amounts before any adjustment`'s `range 4 minimum`)
    AND `possible` (`amounts`'s `range 5 minimum`) (`the amounts before any adjustment`'s `range 5 minimum`)
    AND `possible` (`amounts`'s `range 6 minimum`) (`the amounts before any adjustment`'s `range 6 minimum`)
    AND `possible` (`amounts`'s `premium threshold`) (`the amounts before any adjustment`'s `premium threshold`)
    WHERE
        `possible` `x` `base` MEANS
            `x` AT LEAST `base` AND FLOOR (`x` DIVIDED BY 1000) TIMES 1000 EQUALS `x`

-- The amounts for the year in which liability arose (s 12): the deposited table for 2019-20; for a later year, the
-- table built under s 33AD from that year's adjustable amounts (from s 33AC, or the s 33AF notice); before 1 July 2019,
-- none in the deposit.
DECLARE `Rate amounts` HAS
    `table` IS A LIST OF `Threshold range`
    `premium threshold` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Rate amounts answer` IS ONE OF
    `the rate amounts are` HAS `amounts` IS A `Rate amounts`
    `no rate amounts` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN `the day liability arose` IS A DATE, `the year's amounts` IS AN `Adjustable amounts`
GIVETH A `Rate amounts answer`
`the rate amounts for` MEANS
    IF `the financial year of` `the day liability arose` LESS THAN 2019
    THEN `no rate amounts` `the liability arose before 1 July 2019, before the s 32 table in the deposit applied`
    ELSE IF `the financial year of` `the day liability arose` EQUALS 2019
         THEN `the rate amounts are` (`Rate amounts` OF `the s 32 table as deposited`, (`the amounts before any adjustment`'s `premium threshold`))
         ELSE IF `the amounts could be amounts adjusted under s 33AC` `the year's amounts`
              THEN `the rate amounts are` (`Rate amounts` OF (`the general rate table for` `the year's amounts`), (`the year's amounts`'s `premium threshold`))
              ELSE `no rate amounts` `the amounts given for the year cannot be amounts adjusted under s 33AC`

§§ `s 32A -- the premium rate for residential land`

-- s 32A(1): residential land with a dutiable value exceeding $3,040,000 pays "the premium base amount plus $7 for every
-- $100, or part, by which the dutiable value of the residential land exceeds $3,040,000". (2): the premium base amount is
-- the s 32 duty on $3,040,000 ($152,502 for 2019-20, the note says). (2A): at or below, s 32. (2C): $3,040,000 is an
-- adjustable amount. (5): not where s 32B or s 32C applies.
--
-- s 32A(3): residential land is "(a) a parcel of land on which there is one single dwelling or one flat, or ... a building
-- under construction that, when completed, will constitute one single dwelling or one flat, or (b) a strata lot, if it is
-- lawfully occupied as a separate dwelling, or suitable ..., or (c) a land use entitlement ..., or (d) a parcel of vacant
-- land that is zoned ... for residential or principally for residential purposes." "single dwelling" excludes "a property
-- commonly known as a shop and dwelling" (s 32A(6)). A second occupancy that is an "excluded residential occupancy" (one
-- room, one flat and so on, s 32A(4), (6)) does not stop land being land with one dwelling.
DECLARE `What is on the land` IS ONE OF
    `one house or one flat`
    `one house or one flat, and a shop`
    `a building under construction that will be one house or one flat`
    `a strata lot occupied or suitable as a separate dwelling`
    `vacant land zoned for residential use`
    `two or more dwellings`
    `other land`

GIVEN `the land` IS A `What is on the land`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is residential land for the premium rate` IF
    CONSIDER `the land`
    WHEN `one house or one flat` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a building under construction that will be one house or one flat` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a strata lot occupied or suitable as a separate dwelling` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `vacant land zoned for residential use` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `amounts` IS A `Rate amounts`, `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER, `residential` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the duty at the general or premium rate` MEANS
    IF `residential` AND `the dutiable value` GREATER THAN `amounts`'s `premium threshold`
    THEN `the duty at the general rate on` (`amounts`'s `table`) (`amounts`'s `premium threshold`)
         PLUS 7 TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`the dutiable value` MINUS `amounts`'s `premium threshold`)
    ELSE `the duty at the general rate on` (`amounts`'s `table`) `the dutiable value`

-- The transfer duty on one parcel (one dutiable transaction), before any concession or exemption. s 32B (the Chief
-- Commissioner is satisfied that residential land above the threshold is used for other purposes) and s 32C (a parcel of
-- more than 2 hectares above the threshold) are not encoded and answer `not covered`.
GIVEN `the day liability arose` IS A DATE
      `the year's amounts` IS AN `Adjustable amounts`
      `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER
      `the land` IS A `What is on the land`
      `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it is used for other purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parcel is more than 2 hectares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
`the transfer duty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the rate amounts for` `the day liability arose` `the year's amounts`
    WHEN `no rate amounts` `why` THEN `not covered` `why`
    WHEN `the rate amounts are` `amounts` THEN
        IF `it is residential land for the premium rate` `the land`
           AND `the dutiable value` GREATER THAN `amounts`'s `premium threshold`
           AND `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it is used for other purposes`
        THEN `not covered` `s 32B applies: residential land above the premium threshold used for other purposes; its apportionment factor is not encoded`
        ELSE IF `it is residential land for the premium rate` `the land`
                AND `the dutiable value` GREATER THAN `amounts`'s `premium threshold`
                AND `the parcel is more than 2 hectares`
             THEN `not covered` `s 32C applies: a parcel of residential land of more than 2 hectares above the premium threshold; not encoded`
             ELSE `the duty is` (`the duty at the general or premium rate` `amounts` `the dutiable value` (`it is residential land for the premium rate` `the land`))

§§ `ss 8, 11, 12, 13 and 14 -- what is charged, when, and on whom`

-- s 8(1): duty is charged on "(a) a transfer of dutiable property" and "(b)(i) an agreement for the sale or transfer of
-- dutiable property". s 11(1)(a): "land in New South Wales" is dutiable property.
GIVEN `the land is in New South Wales` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the land is dutiable property` IF `the land is in New South Wales`

-- s 12(1)-(2): liability arises when the transfer occurs, but if it "is effected by an instrument, ... when the instrument
-- is first executed". (s 12(4), electronic registry instruments, is not encoded.) s 13: "Duty ... is payable by the
-- transferee". s 14: "joint tenants of dutiable property are taken to hold the dutiable property as tenants in common in
-- equal shares".

-- A purchaser or transferee, with the facts Part 8 Division 1 and Chapter 2A ask about them.
DECLARE `Kind of purchaser` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a company or a partnership`
    `a trustee`

DECLARE Purchaser HAS
    `kind` IS A `Kind of purchaser`
    `the s 73(2) trustee exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has owned residential property in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has been a party to an approved application under the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the spouse has owned residential property in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the spouse has been a party to an approved application under the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
    `age` IS A NUMBER
    `is an Australian citizen or a permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an approved equity partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a foreign person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a permanent resident or a retirement visa holder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `share` IS A NUMBER

-- s 14: joint tenants hold equal shares; tenants in common hold the shares stated (as percentages).
GIVEN `purchasers` IS A LIST OF Purchaser
      `as joint tenants` IS A BOOLEAN, `the purchaser` IS A Purchaser
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the share taken to be held by` MEANS
    IF `as joint tenants` AND count `purchasers` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN 100 DIVIDED BY count `purchasers`
    ELSE `the purchaser`'s `share`

§§ `Part 8 Division 1 -- the First Home Buyers Assistance Scheme`

-- s 71(2): "A first home owner is an individual-- (a) who has not at any time owned residential property in Australia
-- (either solely or with someone else) and has not previously been a party to an application under the scheme that was
-- approved ..., and (b) whose spouse (if any) has not at any time owned residential property ... and has not previously
-- been a party to an application ... approved". (4): spouse = legally married, or living together as a couple in a de
-- facto relationship; (5): not a husband or wife from whom the purchaser is separated with no intention of resuming
-- cohabitation, if the Chief Commissioner is satisfied of that; (6): property held only as trustee or executor is
-- disregarded; (8): an ACT Commonwealth leasehold counts as owned. Those readings belong to the facts.
-- s 80A: residential property is "(a) land on which there is a building that is lawfully occupied as a place of residence
-- or suitable for occupation as a place of residence, or (b) a company title dwelling".
-- A s 73(2) trustee is eligible when the person it acts for is a first home owner; for such a trustee the ownership facts
-- are that person's (READING: s 71 and s 73(2) do not say whose facts are tested).
GIVEN `the purchaser` IS A Purchaser
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purchaser is a first home owner` IF
        (    CONSIDER `the purchaser`'s `kind`
             WHEN `an individual` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `a trustee` THEN `the purchaser`'s `the s 73(2) trustee exception applies`
             OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND (NOT (`the purchaser`'s `has owned residential property in Australia`))
    AND (NOT (`the purchaser`'s `has been a party to an approved application under the scheme`))
    AND (    (NOT (`the purchaser`'s `has a spouse`))
          OR (    (NOT (`the purchaser`'s `the spouse has owned residential property in Australia`))
              AND (NOT (`the purchaser`'s `the spouse has been a party to an approved application under the scheme`))))

-- s 71(7): a purchaser who is not a first home owner does not stop the agreement being eligible if "(a) one or more of
-- the purchasers or transferees ... is a first home owner, and (b) the total ownership share ... being acquired by
-- purchasers or transferees who are not first home owners does not exceed 5%". (Approved equity partners are left out of
-- the count: s 73A(2) makes their eligibility irrelevant.)
GIVEN `purchasers` IS A LIST OF Purchaser
      `as joint tenants` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 5% allowance in s 71(7) applies` IF
        any (GIVEN `p` YIELD `the purchaser is a first home owner` `p`) `purchasers`
    AND sum (map (GIVEN `p` YIELD `the share of a non-first home owner` `p`) `purchasers`) AT MOST 5
    WHERE
        `the share of a non-first home owner` `p` MEANS
            IF `the purchaser is a first home owner` `p` OR `p`'s `is an approved equity partner`
            THEN 0
            ELSE `the share taken to be held by` `purchasers` `as joint tenants` `p`

-- s 73(5): "not eligible unless the person is an Australian citizen or a permanent resident"; (6): if there is more than
-- one purchaser "and at least one of them is a first home owner who is an Australian citizen or permanent resident, the
-- other purchasers ... are exempt". "permanent resident" (Dictionary): a permanent visa holder, or a New Zealand citizen
-- on a special category visa.
GIVEN `purchasers` IS A LIST OF Purchaser
      `the purchaser` IS A Purchaser
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purchaser meets the citizenship requirement` IF
        `the purchaser`'s `is an Australian citizen or a permanent resident`
    OR  (    count `purchasers` GREATER THAN 1
         AND any (GIVEN `p` YIELD `the purchaser is a first home owner` `p` AND `p`'s `is an Australian citizen or a permanent resident`) `purchasers`)

DECLARE `Why not eligible` IS ONE OF
    `a purchaser is not a first home owner, and the 5% allowance in s 71(7) does not apply`
    `a purchaser is a company, a partnership or a trustee (s 73(1))`
    `a purchaser is under 18 (s 73(3)), unless the Chief Commissioner determines otherwise under s 73(4)`
    `a purchaser is not an Australian citizen or permanent resident (s 73(5))`
    `the agreement is not for a first home, or for a vacant block to be the site of one, to be lived in (s 74(1), s 76)`
    `the agreement is not for the whole of the property (s 74(2))`
    `the dutiable value is not less than the cap in s 74(3)`
    `the agreement involves a business or business premises (s 75(1))`
    `the property is a holiday home (s 75(2))`
    `the agreement was entered into before 1 July 2017 (s 70)`

GIVEN `the purchaser` IS A Purchaser
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purchaser is an individual` IF
    CONSIDER `the purchaser`'s `kind`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 73(1): "Companies, partnerships, and persons in their capacity as trustees, are not eligible." (2): a trustee is
-- eligible if it is the guardian of a first home owner under a legal disability who will occupy the home, or an apparent
-- purchaser (s 55) for a real purchaser who is a first home owner: one fact.
GIVEN `the purchaser` IS A Purchaser
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purchaser is excluded by s 73(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the purchaser`'s `kind`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a trustee` THEN NOT (`the purchaser`'s `the s 73(2) trustee exception applies`)
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Why one purchaser is not eligible (s 71(1), s 73), or nothing if they are. An approved equity partner under an approved
-- shared equity scheme does not need to be eligible (s 73A(2)).
GIVEN `purchasers` IS A LIST OF Purchaser
      `as joint tenants` IS A BOOLEAN, `the purchaser` IS A Purchaser
GIVETH A MAYBE `Why not eligible`
`why the purchaser is not eligible` MEANS
    IF `the purchaser`'s `is an approved equity partner`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF (NOT (`the purchaser is a first home owner` `the purchaser`)) AND (NOT (`the 5% allowance in s 71(7) applies` `purchasers` `as joint tenants`))
         THEN JUST `a purchaser is not a first home owner, and the 5% allowance in s 71(7) does not apply`
         ELSE IF `the purchaser is excluded by s 73(1)` `the purchaser`
              THEN JUST `a purchaser is a company, a partnership or a trustee (s 73(1))`
              ELSE IF `the purchaser is an individual` `the purchaser` AND `the purchaser`'s `age` LESS THAN 18
                   THEN JUST `a purchaser is under 18 (s 73(3)), unless the Chief Commissioner determines otherwise under s 73(4)`
                   ELSE IF NOT (`the purchaser meets the citizenship requirement` `purchasers` `the purchaser`)
                        THEN JUST `a purchaser is not an Australian citizen or permanent resident (s 73(5))`
                        ELSE NOTHING

-- s 73A(1): with more than one purchaser, the agreement "will be eligible under the scheme only if all of the purchasers
-- or transferees are eligible under the scheme".
GIVEN `purchasers` IS A LIST OF Purchaser
      `as joint tenants` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Why not eligible`
`why some purchaser is not eligible` MEANS
    firstJust (map (GIVEN `p` YIELD `why the purchaser is not eligible` `purchasers` `as joint tenants` `p`) `purchasers`)

-- One agreement or transfer under the scheme.
DECLARE `Home purchase` HAS
    `the day of the agreement or transfer` IS A DATE
    `the consideration` IS A NUMBER
    `the unencumbered value` IS A NUMBER
    `the land` IS A `What is on the land`
    `is for the whole of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `involves a business or business premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a holiday home` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a first home owner intends to live in it as a principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is under an approved shared equity scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the purchasers` IS A LIST OF Purchaser
    `as joint tenants` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 74(3): the dutiable value "must be less than-- (a) $1,000,000 if the property has a private dwelling built on it, or
-- (b) $450,000 if the property comprises a vacant block of residential land." s 78A(1): no duty if it "is not more than"
-- $800,000 (a private dwelling) or $350,000 (a vacant block). A strata lot or a house (with or without a shop) has a
-- private dwelling on it; vacant residential land is a vacant block.
DECLARE `Scheme case` IS ONE OF
    `a property with a private dwelling built on it`
    `a vacant block of residential land`
    `neither case plainly`
    `not a home or residential land`

GIVEN `the land` IS A `What is on the land`
GIVETH A `Scheme case`
`the scheme case of` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the land`
    WHEN `one house or one flat` THEN `a property with a private dwelling built on it`
    WHEN `one house or one flat, and a shop` THEN `a property with a private dwelling built on it`
    WHEN `a strata lot occupied or suitable as a separate dwelling` THEN `a property with a private dwelling built on it`
    WHEN `vacant land zoned for residential use` THEN `a vacant block of residential land`
    WHEN `a building under construction that will be one house or one flat` THEN `neither case plainly`
    WHEN `two or more dwellings` THEN `neither case plainly`
    WHEN `other land` THEN `not a home or residential land`

GIVEN `the case` IS A `Scheme case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 74(3) cap for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the case`
    WHEN `a vacant block of residential land` THEN 450000
    OTHERWISE 1000000

GIVEN `the case` IS A `Scheme case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 78A(1) nil-duty limit for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the case`
    WHEN `a vacant block of residential land` THEN 350000
    OTHERWISE 800000

GIVEN `the purchase` IS A `Home purchase`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the dutiable value of the purchase` MEANS
    `the dutiable value of the property` (`the purchase`'s `the consideration`) (`the purchase`'s `the unencumbered value`)

-- s 70: eligible are "(a) agreements for sale or transfer entered into on or after 1 July 2017, (b) transfers that occur on
-- or after 1 July 2017". Schedule 1 cl 147(1): the First Home Buyer Legislation Amendment Act 2023 applies to agreements
-- entered into, and transfers, on or after 1 July 2023; (3): the Act as in force before it applies to the others. The
-- deposit does not say which provisions that Act changed, so every earlier agreement is `not covered`.
-- The transaction tests, in the Act's order: s 74(1), (2), (3), s 75(1), (2). s 76 (the residence requirement) is met in
-- advance by the intention fact (s 76A(1)), or does not apply (s 76(6)); for a vacant block it is enough that the Chief
-- Commissioner is satisfied it is intended as the site of a home (s 76(3)).
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A `Home purchase`, `the residence requirement applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Why not eligible`
`why the agreement is not eligible` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the day is on or after` (`the purchase`'s `the day of the agreement or transfer`) 1 7 2017)
    THEN JUST `the agreement was entered into before 1 July 2017 (s 70)`
    ELSE IF (CONSIDER `the scheme case of` (`the purchase`'s `the land`)
             WHEN `not a home or residential land` THEN TRUE
             OTHERWISE FALSE)
            OR (`the residence requirement applies` AND (NOT (`the purchase`'s `a first home owner intends to live in it as a principal place of residence`)))
         THEN JUST `the agreement is not for a first home, or for a vacant block to be the site of one, to be lived in (s 74(1), s 76)`
         ELSE IF NOT (`the purchase`'s `is for the whole of the property`)
              THEN JUST `the agreement is not for the whole of the property (s 74(2))`
              ELSE IF `the dutiable value of the purchase` `the purchase` AT LEAST `the s 74(3) cap for` (`the scheme case of` (`the purchase`'s `the land`))
                   THEN JUST `the dutiable value is not less than the cap in s 74(3)`
                   ELSE IF `the purchase`'s `involves a business or business premises`
                        THEN JUST `the agreement involves a business or business premises (s 75(1))`
                        ELSE IF `the purchase`'s `is a holiday home`
                             THEN JUST `the property is a holiday home (s 75(2))`
                             ELSE NOTHING

-- s 78B(1)-(2): where one or more purchasers is a first home owner but the agreement fails only because another purchaser
-- is not eligible, there may be a shared equity concession if "(a) the purchasers ... who are first home owners must
-- acquire not less than a 50% share", and (b) it "would be eligible under the scheme if the first home owners were the
-- sole purchasers". (6): not under an approved shared equity scheme. The formula in s 78B(3) is missing (see below).
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A `Home purchase`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the shared equity concession is in play` IF
        (NOT (`the purchase`'s `is under an approved shared equity scheme`))
    AND count `the first home owners` GREATER THAN 0
    AND isNothing (`why some purchaser is not eligible` `the first home owners` FALSE)
    AND sum (map (GIVEN `p` YIELD `the share taken to be held by` (`the purchase`'s `the purchasers`) (`the purchase`'s `as joint tenants`) `p`) `the first home owners`) AT LEAST 50
    WHERE
        `the first home owners` MEANS filter (GIVEN `p` YIELD `the purchaser is a first home owner` `p`) (`the purchase`'s `the purchasers`)

DECLARE `First home buyer answer` IS ONE OF
    `no duty is chargeable under s 78A(1), once the Chief Commissioner approves the application`
    `not eligible under the scheme` HAS `because` IS A `Why not eligible`
    `not covered under the scheme` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

-- s 78A(1): "If an application concerning an eligible agreement or transfer is approved and the dutiable value ... is not
-- more than the following amounts, no duty is chargeable". (2), (2A): above that, "the rate of duty ... is to be
-- calculated in accordance with the following formula--" and the formula is an image the corpus dropped; only "N ... V ...
-- D ..." survive. So the concessional band ($800,000 to $1,000,000 for a home, $350,000 to $450,000 for a vacant block)
-- is `not covered`. The same for s 78B(3): only "D ... R ... E ... C ..." survive.
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A `Home purchase`, `the residence requirement applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `First home buyer answer`
`the first home buyer answer` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the day is on or after` (`the purchase`'s `the day of the agreement or transfer`) 1 7 2023)
    THEN `not covered under the scheme` `the agreement or transfer is before 1 July 2023, to which the Act as in force before the First Home Buyer Legislation Amendment Act 2023 applies (Schedule 1 cl 147(3)); not deposited`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the scheme case of` (`the purchase`'s `the land`)
         WHEN `neither case plainly` THEN `not covered under the scheme` `the land has a building under construction or more than one dwelling, which the scheme's two cases (a private dwelling, a vacant block) do not plainly cover`
         OTHERWISE
             CONSIDER `why the agreement is not eligible` `the purchase` `the residence requirement applies`
             WHEN JUST `why` THEN `not eligible under the scheme` `why`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN
                 CONSIDER `why some purchaser is not eligible` (`the purchase`'s `the purchasers`) (`the purchase`'s `as joint tenants`)
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN
                     IF `the dutiable value of the purchase` `the purchase` AT MOST `the s 78A(1) nil-duty limit for` (`the scheme case of` (`the purchase`'s `the land`))
                     THEN `no duty is chargeable under s 78A(1), once the Chief Commissioner approves the application`
                     ELSE `not covered under the scheme` `the s 78A(2) or (2A) concessional duty formula is missing from the deposited text`
                 WHEN JUST `why` THEN
                     IF `the shared equity concession is in play` `the purchase`
                     THEN `not covered under the scheme` `the s 78B(3) shared equity concession formula is missing from the deposited text`
                     ELSE `not eligible under the scheme` `why`

-- The duty a first home buyer pays: nil under s 78A(1); otherwise, if not eligible, the duty at the general or premium
-- rate on the agreement (the scheme does not apply).
GIVEN `the purchase` IS A `Home purchase`
      `the residence requirement applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the year's amounts` IS AN `Adjustable amounts`
      `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it is used for other purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parcel is more than 2 hectares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
`the duty for a first home buyer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the first home buyer answer` `the purchase` `the residence requirement applies`
    WHEN `no duty is chargeable under s 78A(1), once the Chief Commissioner approves the application` THEN `the duty is` 0
    WHEN `not covered under the scheme` `why` THEN `not covered` `why`
    WHEN `not eligible under the scheme` `why` THEN
        `the transfer duty` (`the purchase`'s `the day of the agreement or transfer`) `the year's amounts`
            (`the dutiable value of the purchase` `the purchase`) (`the purchase`'s `the land`)
            `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it is used for other purposes` `the parcel is more than 2 hectares`

-- s 76(1): "The home must be occupied by the first home owner or one of the first home owners who is acquiring it as a
-- principal place of residence for a continuous period of at least 12 months, with that occupation starting within 12
-- months (or such longer period as the Chief Commissioner may approve) after completion". (2): the Chief Commissioner may
-- approve a shorter period, or exempt. (5): completion is when the purchaser is entitled to possession and the interest is
-- registered. (6): the requirement "does not apply ... if, on the date of the agreement or transfer-- (a) the applicant
-- or ... at least one of the applicants is a member of the Permanent Forces of the Australian Defence Force ..., and (b)
-- ... each of the applicants is enrolled to vote in State elections".
`the months allowed to start living in the home` MEANS 12
`the months of continuous occupation required` MEANS 12

GIVEN `an applicant is in the Permanent Forces and each applicant is enrolled to vote in NSW` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Chief Commissioner has exempted the first home owner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the residence requirement applies` IF
        (NOT (`an applicant is in the Permanent Forces and each applicant is enrolled to vote in NSW`))
    AND (NOT (`the Chief Commissioner has exempted the first home owner`))

GIVEN `the requirement applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a first home owner moved in` IS A BOOLEAN
      `months from completion to moving in` IS A NUMBER
      `months of continuous occupation` IS A NUMBER
      `months allowed to start` IS A NUMBER
      `months of occupation required` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the residence requirement is complied with` IF
        (NOT `the requirement applies`)
    OR  (    `a first home owner moved in`
         AND `months from completion to moving in` AT MOST `months allowed to start`
         AND `months of continuous occupation` AT LEAST `months of occupation required`)

-- s 76A(3): "The relevant duty is the difference between the total amount of duty that would have been payable on the
-- transactions and instruments the subject of the application, if they had not been eligible under the scheme, and the
-- total amount of duty (if any) paid in respect of those transactions and instruments."
GIVEN `the duty if not eligible` IS A `Duty answer`, `the duty paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
`the relevant duty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the duty if not eligible`
    WHEN `the duty is` `d` THEN `the duty is` (`d` MINUS `the duty paid`)
    WHEN `not covered` `why` THEN `not covered` `why`

-- s 76A(2): the 14 days run from "the end of the period allowed for compliance". READING: the Act does not define that
-- period; it is taken to end when the period allowed to start living in the home ends (12 months after completion, or the
-- longer period the Chief Commissioner approved).
`the days allowed to notify and pay` MEANS 14

GIVEN `the day of completion` IS A DATE, `months allowed to start` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of the period allowed for compliance` MEANS
    `the day that is` `the day of completion` `months allowed to start`

GIVEN `the day of completion` IS A DATE, `months allowed to start` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to give notice and pay the relevant duty` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL (`the end of the period allowed for compliance` `the day of completion` `months allowed to start`) PLUS `the days allowed to notify and pay`)

-- s 76A(2) binds only an applicant whose application was approved in anticipation of compliance, and only "if the
-- residence requirement is not complied with".
GIVEN `it was approved in anticipation of the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the residence requirement was complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 76A(2) condition binds the applicant` IF
    `it was approved in anticipation of the residence requirement` AND (NOT `the residence requirement was complied with`)

§§ `Part 8 Division 4 -- transfers between spouses`

-- s 104A(1): residential land is "(a) a parcel of land on which there is-- (i) one single dwelling or one flat, or (ii) one
-- single dwelling, or one flat, and a shop, or (iii) a building under construction ..., or (b) a strata lot ..., or (c) a
-- land use entitlement ..., or (d) a parcel of vacant land ... zoned ... for residential ... purposes".
GIVEN `the land` IS A `What is on the land`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is residential land for the spouse exemption` IF
    CONSIDER `the land`
    WHEN `two or more dwellings` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `other land` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- "de facto partner" (Dictionary): "a person who has been a party to a de facto relationship for a period of not less than
-- 2 years"; s 104B(1)(e): "in the case of de facto partners, the parties ... have lived in the relationship for at least 2
-- years before the date of the transfer".
DECLARE `The couple` IS ONE OF
    `a married couple`
    `de facto partners who have lived in the relationship for at least 2 years`
    `de facto partners for less than 2 years`
    `not a couple`

DECLARE `Spouse transfer` HAS
    `the land` IS A `What is on the land`
    `the couple` IS A `The couple`
    `afterwards the couple hold it as joint tenants or tenants in common in equal shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is the couple's principal place of residence, or the intended site of it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is used solely for residential purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the only parties are the couple` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 104B(1): "No duty is chargeable under this Chapter on a transfer, or an agreement for the sale or transfer, of
-- residential land if-- (a) as a result ..., the property is or will be held by a married couple or de facto partners as
-- joint tenants or as tenants in common in equal shares, and (b) ... (i) ... a dwelling that, when the transfer ...
-- occurs, is used as the principal place of residence of the married couple or de facto partners, or (ii) ... vacant land,
-- or ... a building under construction, and [they] intend to use [it] as the site of a dwelling to be used as their
-- principal place of residence, and (c) the residential land is used solely for residential purposes ..., and (d) both
-- the transferor and the transferee are the married couple or one of them ... and no other person is a party to the
-- transfer, and (e) [de facto: 2 years]." (2): one room used for a business conducted mainly elsewhere is disregarded.
-- (3): land partly held by someone else may still be exempt.
GIVEN `the transfer` IS A `Spouse transfer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the couple test in s 104B(1)(e) is met` IF
    CONSIDER `the transfer`'s `the couple`
    WHEN `a married couple` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `de facto partners who have lived in the relationship for at least 2 years` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the transfer` IS A `Spouse transfer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 104B holds but for the use of the land` IF
        `it is residential land for the spouse exemption` (`the transfer`'s `the land`)
    AND `the transfer`'s `afterwards the couple hold it as joint tenants or tenants in common in equal shares`
    AND `the transfer`'s `it is the couple's principal place of residence, or the intended site of it`
    AND `the transfer`'s `the only parties are the couple`
    AND `the couple test in s 104B(1)(e) is met` `the transfer`

GIVEN `the transfer` IS A `Spouse transfer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer is exempt under s 104B` IF
        `s 104B holds but for the use of the land` `the transfer`
    AND `the transfer`'s `it is used solely for residential purposes`

-- s 104C(1): if the transfer "would be exempt from duty under section 104B, but for the fact that the land has been used or
-- is intended to be used for a purpose other than a residential purpose, the duty ... is to be calculated after reducing
-- the dutiable value of the land by the residential apportionment factor." (2): that factor is 1 minus the non-residential
-- apportionment factor, which (3)-(5) take from the Register of Land Values or the Chief Commissioner: an INPUT here.
-- (6): "at the general rate provided for by section 32. Sections 32A-32C do not apply."
-- READING: "reducing the dutiable value ... by the residential apportionment factor" takes the residential share off, so
-- the duty falls on the dutiable value times the non-residential apportionment factor.
GIVEN `the transfer` IS A `Spouse transfer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 104C concession applies` IF
        `s 104B holds but for the use of the land` `the transfer`
    AND (NOT (`the transfer`'s `it is used solely for residential purposes`))

GIVEN `the transfer` IS A `Spouse transfer`
      `the day liability arose` IS A DATE
      `the year's amounts` IS AN `Adjustable amounts`
      `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER
      `the non-residential apportionment factor` IS A NUMBER
      `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it is used for other purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parcel is more than 2 hectares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
`the duty on a transfer between spouses` MEANS
    IF `the transfer is exempt under s 104B` `the transfer`
    THEN `the duty is` 0
    ELSE IF `the s 104C concession applies` `the transfer`
         THEN CONSIDER `the rate amounts for` `the day liability arose` `the year's amounts`
              WHEN `no rate amounts` `why` THEN `not covered` `why`
              WHEN `the rate amounts are` `amounts` THEN
                  `the duty is` (`the duty at the general rate on` (`amounts`'s `table`)
                                     (`the dutiable value` MINUS `the dutiable value` TIMES (1 MINUS `the non-residential apportionment factor`)))
         ELSE `the transfer duty` `the day liability arose` `the year's amounts` `the dutiable value` (`the transfer`'s `the land`)
                  `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it is used for other purposes` `the parcel is more than 2 hectares`

§§ `Chapter 2A -- surcharge purchaser duty`

-- s 104G(2): surcharge purchaser duty "is additional to any duty charged by Chapter 2". s 104L(1)(a), (b)(i): it is charged
-- on a transfer, or an agreement for the transfer, "of residential-related property to a foreign person"; s 104K(a):
-- residential-related property includes "residential land in New South Wales". s 104I: residential land is a parcel with
-- one or more dwellings (or a building under construction that will be), a strata lot, a utility lot, a land use
-- entitlement or residential-zoned vacant land, "and does not include any land used for primary production".
-- s 104J: "foreign person" is the FATA meaning, modified so that an Australian citizen is ordinarily resident and a New
-- Zealand citizen on a special category visa is not time-limited: a FACT. (3): tested when Chapter 2 liability arises.
GIVEN `the land` IS A `What is on the land`, `it is used for primary production` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is residential land for surcharge purchaser duty` IF
        (NOT `it is used for primary production`)
    AND (CONSIDER `the land`
         WHEN `other land` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

-- s 104U(1): "a rate of 9% of the dutiable value"; (2): "If any of the transferees are not foreign persons, surcharge
-- purchaser duty is to be charged only on the proportion of the dutiable value ... that is the same as the proportion of
-- the share or shares ... transferred to foreign persons." s 104V applies s 14 (joint tenants hold equal shares).
-- s 104Z applies s 21: the dutiable value is the greater of the consideration and the unencumbered value.
-- s 104R: "(1) The person liable to pay surcharge purchaser duty is the transferee. (2) Only transferees who are foreign
-- persons are liable". s 104ZK(2): the Part 8 exemptions and concessions (the scheme, s 104B) do not apply to it.
-- Schedule 1 cl 156: the 9% rate (as amended by the Revenue Legislation Amendment Act 2024) applies to a transaction
-- after its commencement, which the deposit does not date; the text is in force at its version date, 1 January 2025.
GIVEN `purchasers` IS A LIST OF Purchaser
      `as joint tenants` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the share transferred to foreign persons` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN `p` YIELD IF `p`'s `is a foreign person` THEN `the share taken to be held by` `purchasers` `as joint tenants` `p` ELSE 0) `purchasers`)

GIVEN `the day liability arose` IS A DATE
      `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER
      `the land` IS A `What is on the land`
      `it is used for primary production` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it is used for other purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `purchasers` IS A LIST OF Purchaser
      `as joint tenants` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
`the surcharge purchaser duty` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`it is residential land for surcharge purchaser duty` `the land` `it is used for primary production`))
       OR (NOT (any (GIVEN `p` YIELD `p`'s `is a foreign person`) `purchasers`))
    THEN `the duty is` 0
    ELSE IF NOT (`the day is on or after` `the day liability arose` 1 1 2025)
         THEN `not covered` `the surcharge liability arose before 1 January 2025, the version date of the deposit; the commencement of the 9% rate is not in the deposit`
         ELSE IF any (GIVEN `p` YIELD `p`'s `is a foreign person` AND `p`'s `is a permanent resident or a retirement visa holder`) `purchasers`
              THEN `not covered` `a foreign transferee may be an exempt permanent resident or retirement visa holder (s 104ZKA, s 104ZKB); not encoded`
              ELSE IF `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it is used for other purposes`
                   THEN `not covered` `the land is used for other purposes and the s 104ZB apportionment factor is not encoded`
                   ELSE `the duty is` (`the dutiable value` TIMES 9 DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES `the share transferred to foreign persons` `purchasers` `as joint tenants` DIVIDED BY 100)

-- s 104R(2): "Only transferees who are foreign persons are liable to pay surcharge purchaser duty." The duty a given
-- transferee is liable for: none if not a foreign person; otherwise the duty charged on the transaction (on the foreign
-- shares). READING: how the liability is shared between several foreign transferees is left to the Taxation
-- Administration Act 1996 (not deposited); the whole amount is returned.
GIVEN `the transferee` IS A Purchaser
      `the day liability arose` IS A DATE
      `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER
      `the land` IS A `What is on the land`
      `it is used for primary production` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it is used for other purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `purchasers` IS A LIST OF Purchaser
      `as joint tenants` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
`the surcharge purchaser duty the transferee is liable for` MEANS
    IF `the transferee`'s `is a foreign person`
    THEN `the surcharge purchaser duty` `the day liability arose` `the dutiable value` `the land` `it is used for primary production`
             `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it is used for other purposes` `purchasers` `as joint tenants`
    ELSE `the duty is` 0

§§ `Chapter 9 -- motor vehicle registration duty`

-- s 261: duty is charged "on an application to register a motor vehicle under the Road Transport Act 2013 if-- (a) the
-- vehicle has not previously been registered under that Act, or (b) the person in whose name the vehicle is to be
-- registered differs ... from the person or persons in whose name or names the vehicle was last registered." An
-- "application to register" includes an application to transfer the registration (Dictionary).
GIVEN `it has been registered under the Road Transport Act 2013 before` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to be registered in the same name or names as last registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application is charged with duty under s 261` IF
        (NOT `it has been registered under the Road Transport Act 2013 before`)
    OR  (NOT `it is to be registered in the same name or names as last registered`)

-- s 266(1): the dutiable value is "(a) the consideration in money or money's worth given for the acquisition of the
-- vehicle, or (b) the market value of the vehicle at the time duty is payable, whichever is the greater." (2): it "does
-- not include-- (a) GST if the supply of the vehicle is GST-free under Subdivision 38-P (Cars for use by disabled people)
-- of the A New Tax System (Goods and Services Tax) Act 1999 ..., or (b) a premium paid for extended warranty insurance."
-- READING: the amounts in (2) are taken off the greater figure, which is assumed to include them.
GIVEN `the consideration` IS A NUMBER
      `the market value` IS A NUMBER
      `GST excluded by s 266(2)(a)` IS A NUMBER
      `an extended warranty premium included` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the dutiable value of the vehicle` MEANS
    `the greater of` `the consideration` `the market value` MINUS `GST excluded by s 266(2)(a)` MINUS `an extended warranty premium included`

-- s 265(2): a passenger vehicle is one "(a) that has a dutiable value of not less than $45,000, and (b) that is constructed
-- primarily for the carriage of not more than 9 occupants, including a sedan, station wagon, coupe, convertible, four
-- wheel drive vehicle with seats and windows, two wheel drive panel van with seats and windows, three wheel car, forward
-- control passenger vehicle, small bus (seating not more than 9 persons, including the driver), motor home, and snow
-- vehicle, but not including a motor cycle ..., large bus ..., hearse or invalid conveyance".
DECLARE `Kind of vehicle` IS ONE OF
    `a vehicle constructed primarily to carry not more than 9 occupants`
    `a motor cycle`
    `a bus seating more than 9 persons`
    `a hearse or an invalid conveyance`
    `another vehicle`

GIVEN `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER, `the kind` IS A `Kind of vehicle`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a passenger vehicle under s 265(2)` IF
        `the dutiable value` AT LEAST 45000
    AND (CONSIDER `the kind`
         WHEN `a vehicle constructed primarily to carry not more than 9 occupants` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

-- s 265(1): "$3 per $100, or part, of the dutiable value"; (2): a passenger vehicle pays "$1,350 plus $5 per $100, or part,
-- of the dutiable value of the motor vehicle in excess of $45,000".
GIVEN `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER, `the kind` IS A `Kind of vehicle`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the duty at the s 265 rate` MEANS
    IF `it is a passenger vehicle under s 265(2)` `the dutiable value` `the kind`
    THEN 1350 PLUS 5 TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`the dutiable value` MINUS 45000)
    ELSE 3 TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` `the dutiable value`

-- s 267, the exemptions an individual can meet:
-- (1) "made by a person who is beneficially entitled to the vehicle following the death of the person in whose name the
--     vehicle was registered in New South Wales";
-- (6), (6A), (7) a transfer of registration between the parties to a marriage that has been dissolved or annulled or has
--     broken down irretrievably, a de facto relationship that has broken down, or a domestic relationship that has
--     ceased, to the extent the vehicle was matrimonial or relationship property, under a binding financial agreement, a
--     court order or a property division agreement (for a domestic relationship, a court order under the Property
--     (Relationships) Act 1984) -- each "proved to the satisfaction of the Chief Commissioner": answered conditionally;
-- (7A) a veteran "eligible for 70% or more of the general rate of pension specified in section 22 (3)" of the Veterans'
--     Entitlements Act 1986, or for the rate under s 22(4), s 23 or s 24 of that Act;
-- (7AA) a member or former member under the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004 with "at least 50 impairment
--     points" who "is eligible for, in receipt of, or has at any time received compensation or a special rate disability
--     pension under that Act";
-- (7B) a vehicle "to be registered conditionally".
-- s 268: not chargeable if the vehicle "is or was registered by the person making the application under the law of an
-- Australian jurisdiction that corresponds to the Road Transport Act 2013, and ... duty was paid in that jurisdiction".
DECLARE `Veterans' Entitlements Act pension` IS ONE OF
    `none, or less than 70% of the general rate`
    `70% or more of the general rate (s 22(3))`
    `the extreme disablement adjustment rate (s 22(4))`
    `the intermediate rate (s 23)`
    `the special rate (s 24)`

DECLARE `Vehicle exemption facts` HAS
    `the applicant is entitled to it following the death of the registered owner in NSW` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a relationship breakdown transfer within s 267(6), (6A) or (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the veteran's pension` IS A `Veterans' Entitlements Act pension`
    `MRCA impairment points` IS A NUMBER
    `is eligible for, receives or has received MRCA compensation or a special rate disability pension` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is to be registered conditionally` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant registered it in another Australian jurisdiction and paid duty there` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `facts` IS A `Vehicle exemption facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application is exempt under s 267 or s 268` IF
        `facts`'s `the applicant is entitled to it following the death of the registered owner in NSW`
    OR  `facts`'s `it is a relationship breakdown transfer within s 267(6), (6A) or (7)`
    OR  (CONSIDER `facts`'s `the veteran's pension`
         WHEN `none, or less than 70% of the general rate` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)
    OR  (    `facts`'s `MRCA impairment points` AT LEAST 50
         AND `facts`'s `is eligible for, receives or has received MRCA compensation or a special rate disability pension`)
    OR  `facts`'s `it is to be registered conditionally`
    OR  `facts`'s `the applicant registered it in another Australian jurisdiction and paid duty there`

-- An application is chargeable with duty under Chapter 9 if s 261 charges it and no exemption in Part 2 applies.
GIVEN `charged` IS A BOOLEAN, `facts` IS A `Vehicle exemption facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application is chargeable with duty under Chapter 9` IF
    `charged` AND (NOT (`the application is exempt under s 267 or s 268` `facts`))

-- s 263: "Duty is payable by the applicant for registration"; s 264: it "becomes payable when the motor vehicle is
-- registered". This Act sets no period for paying it (the Taxation Administration Act 1996 is not deposited).
GIVEN `charged` IS A BOOLEAN, `facts` IS A `Vehicle exemption facts`, `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER, `the kind` IS A `Kind of vehicle`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the motor vehicle registration duty` MEANS
    IF `the application is chargeable with duty under Chapter 9` `charged` `facts`
    THEN `the duty at the s 265 rate` `the dutiable value` `the kind`
    ELSE 0

§§ `Regulative rules -- the transferee, the applicant under the scheme, and the applicant for registration`

-- Clock: days, counted from the day the rule starts, which each rule names.
DECLARE `Duties party` IS ONE OF
    `the transferee`
    `the applicant under the scheme`
    `the applicant for registration`

DECLARE `Duties act` IS ONE OF
    `make a written statement in the approved form`
    `lodge the instrument or written statement with the Chief Commissioner` HAS `with the purchaser's declaration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `pay the duty` HAS `amount` IS A NUMBER
    `pay the surcharge purchaser duty` HAS `amount` IS A NUMBER
    `give the Chief Commissioner written notice that the residence requirement was not complied with`
    `pay the relevant duty to the Chief Commissioner` HAS `amount` IS A NUMBER
    `lodge a statement of the dutiable value with the application`

-- s 15(1)-(2): if a dutiable transaction liable to ad valorem duty "is not effected by an instrument, the transferee must
-- make a written statement in an approved form ... within 3 months after the liability arises". s 16(1): the transferee
-- "must, within 3 months after the liability arises, lodge with the Chief Commissioner-- (a) the instrument ..., or (b)
-- the written statement". s 16A: the transferee "must lodge a declaration in the approved form with the instrument or
-- written statement". Clock: days from the day liability arose (s 12). (s 15(4), lodging an instrument made within the 3
-- months in place of the statement, is not encoded.)
`the months to lodge and pay` MEANS 3

-- The last day of the 3 months (READING in the Dates section).
GIVEN `the day liability arose` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to lodge and pay` MEANS
    `the day that is` `the day liability arose` `the months to lodge and pay`

GIVEN `the day liability arose` IS A DATE, `it is effected by an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duties party` `Duties act`
DECIDE `ss 15, 16, 16A -- the transferee must lodge the instrument or a written statement, with the purchaser's declaration, within 3 months` IS
    IF `it is effected by an instrument`
    THEN PARTY `the transferee`
         MUST  `lodge the instrument or written statement with the Chief Commissioner` TRUE
         WITHIN `the number of days from the day to` `the day liability arose` `the months to lodge and pay`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the transferee` BECAUSE "ss 16(1), 16A: the transferee must lodge the instrument, with the purchaser's declaration, within 3 months after liability arises"
    ELSE    (PARTY `the transferee`
             MUST  `make a written statement in the approved form`
             WITHIN `the number of days from the day to` `the day liability arose` `the months to lodge and pay`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the transferee` BECAUSE "s 15(1), (2): a transferee whose transaction is not effected by an instrument must make a written statement in the approved form within 3 months after liability arises")
        RAND
            (PARTY `the transferee`
             MUST  `lodge the instrument or written statement with the Chief Commissioner` TRUE
             WITHIN `the number of days from the day to` `the day liability arose` `the months to lodge and pay`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the transferee` BECAUSE "ss 16(1)(b), 16A: the transferee must lodge the written statement, with the purchaser's declaration, within 3 months after liability arises")

-- s 17(1): "A tax default does not occur for the purposes of the Taxation Administration Act 1996 if duty is paid within 3
-- months after the liability to pay the duty arises." Written as a deadline: the breach is a tax default (interest and
-- penalty tax are in the Taxation Administration Act 1996, not deposited). Clock: days from the day liability arose.
GIVEN `the day liability arose` IS A DATE, `the duty` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duties party` `Duties act`
DECIDE `s 17 -- the transferee must pay the duty within 3 months to avoid a tax default` IS
    IF `the duty` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN PARTY `the transferee`
         MUST  `pay the duty` (EXACTLY `the duty`)
         WITHIN `the number of days from the day to` `the day liability arose` `the months to lodge and pay`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the transferee` BECAUSE "s 17(1): duty not paid within 3 months after liability arose; a tax default occurs under the Taxation Administration Act 1996"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 104W: "A tax default does not occur ... if surcharge purchaser duty is paid within 3 months after the liability to pay
-- the duty arises." Only a foreign transferee is liable (s 104R(2)). Clock: days from the day liability arose (s 104Q).
GIVEN `the day liability arose` IS A DATE, `the surcharge` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duties party` `Duties act`
DECIDE `s 104W -- a foreign transferee must pay surcharge purchaser duty within 3 months to avoid a tax default` IS
    IF `the surcharge` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN PARTY `the transferee`
         MUST  `pay the surcharge purchaser duty` (EXACTLY `the surcharge`)
         WITHIN `the number of days from the day to` `the day liability arose` `the months to lodge and pay`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the transferee` BECAUSE "s 104W: surcharge purchaser duty not paid within 3 months after liability arose; a tax default occurs under the Taxation Administration Act 1996"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 76A(2): an approval in anticipation of the residence requirement "is given on condition that, if the residence
-- requirement is not complied with, the applicant must within 14 days after the end of the period allowed for
-- compliance-- (a) give written notice of that fact to the Chief Commissioner, and (b) pay the relevant duty to the Chief
-- Commissioner." (4): failing to is an offence, maximum 50 penalty units; (5): it is a tax default. Clock: days from the
-- end of the period allowed for compliance.
GIVEN `it was approved in anticipation of the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the residence requirement was complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant duty` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duties party` `Duties act`
DECIDE `s 76A(2) -- if the residence requirement is not met, the applicant must give written notice and pay the relevant duty within 14 days` IS
    IF `the s 76A(2) condition binds the applicant` `it was approved in anticipation of the residence requirement` `the residence requirement was complied with`
    THEN    (PARTY `the applicant under the scheme`
             MUST  `give the Chief Commissioner written notice that the residence requirement was not complied with`
             WITHIN `the days allowed to notify and pay`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant under the scheme` BECAUSE "s 76A(2)(a), (4): the applicant must give the Chief Commissioner written notice within 14 days after the period allowed for compliance ends; an offence, maximum 50 penalty units")
        RAND
            (PARTY `the applicant under the scheme`
             MUST  `pay the relevant duty to the Chief Commissioner` (EXACTLY `the relevant duty`)
             WITHIN `the days allowed to notify and pay`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant under the scheme` BECAUSE "s 76A(2)(b), (4), (5): the applicant must pay the relevant duty within 14 days after the period allowed for compliance ends; an offence, maximum 50 penalty units, and a tax default")
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 262: "A person who is required by law to make an application to register a motor vehicle ... must lodge with the
-- application for registration a statement of the dutiable value of the vehicle, unless the application is not
-- chargeable with duty under this Chapter. Maximum penalty--100 penalty units." Clock: days from the application; "with
-- the application" is day 0.
GIVEN `the application is chargeable with duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Duties party` `Duties act`
DECIDE `s 262 -- the applicant for registration must lodge a statement of the dutiable value with the application` IS
    IF `the application is chargeable with duty`
    THEN PARTY `the applicant for registration`
         MUST  `lodge a statement of the dutiable value with the application`
         WITHIN 0
         LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant for registration` BECAUSE "s 262: the applicant must lodge a statement of the dutiable value with the application for registration; maximum penalty 100 penalty units"
    ELSE FULFILLED
